+# To-do app
+
+A minimal local to-do list. Static page, no build step, no server, no dependencies; state lives in `localStorage`. Matches the stack in PROJECT_CONFIG.md.
+
+## Behavior
+
+- Add a task: submit nonblank text. Text is trimmed; blank/whitespace-only input is rejected with an inline error and nothing is added.
+- Complete/incomplete: toggle a task's checkbox.
+- Delete: remove a task.
+- Persistence: tasks and their done state survive a reload via `localStorage` (key `todos.v1`). Corrupt or malformed stored data degrades to an empty list instead of throwing.
+
+## Files
+
+- `index.html` — page markup and styles; mounts the app on `window.localStorage`.
+- `todo.js` — storage-agnostic task store (`TodoStore.createStore`): validation, toggle, delete, persistence. Shared by the page and tests.
+- `app.js` — DOM wiring (`TodoApp.mount(document, storage)`); renders with `textContent` so task text is never interpreted as HTML.
+- `tests/` — executable checks (Node's built-in test runner).
+
+## Run the checks
+
+```
+npm test        # or: node --test
+```
+
+Runs with Node's built-in runner; no install needed.
+
+## Verification notes
+
+Checked on 2026-09-23 (Node v26.3.0):
+
+- `node --test`: 13 passing — store behavior, DOM wiring, persistence across a remount, and that `index.html` exposes the ids/scripts the app expects.
+- Rendered `index.html` in headless Chrome at desktop (520px) and mobile (390px) widths; confirmed layout, empty state, and a populated list with a completed item.
